ins, never re-derive. Per-build note: the warm per-point cost of the Schwinger evaluator is recorded (not gated) in WP2's change report to price the future envelope-surrogate decision.

### WP1: Parity-aware saddle geometry (domain split, centered-source saddle case, two-lobe caustic)
  What: Extend cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/geometry.py to macro-saddle (negative-parity) hosts while leaving positive-parity behavior byte-identical. No evaluator/operator changes here.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/geometry.py
  How: FIRST read negative_parity_research.md Sec 9 (certified domain/refusals) and Sec 11 (build split) for the EXACT lam definition and domain conditions; verify pins, do NOT re-derive or guess the lam sign. (1) macro_matrix: today it raises geometry.LensDomainError when 1-kappa<=|gamma| (positive-parity guard). Split the domain: positive parity (1-kappa>|gamma|) UNCHANGED/byte-identical; ACCEPT saddle (1-kappa<|gamma| with lam>0); raise a NAMED refusal (the existing LensDomainError or a clearly-named subclass, matching the engine's named-refusal contract) for lam<=0 (Type III, OUT of scope) AND for the exact parity boundary. When deciding the boundary use float64-EXACT points per F004 (powers of two, e.g. kappa=0.5/gamma=0.5, kappa=0.75/gamma=0.25) so 1-kappa==|gamma| holds bit-for-bit. (2) _centered_source_images: add the saddle (centered-source) case returning the correct image set and Morse indices on the INDEFINITE Hessian. (3) critical_point / _caustic_source / nearest_caustic_point: emit BOTH 3-cusp deltoid lobes via the +- branch of the EXISTING astroid v(theta') formula (research Fact 1); positive-parity output unchanged; test that the two lobes are distinct, non-overlapping, each with exactly 3 cusps. (4) Hessian / delay / Morse-index / image_kernel: DO NOT modify — research Fact 4 states they already work unmodified on the indefinite matrix; verify by reading, do not edit. Conventions to respect (Professor): Morse index sign e^{-i*pi*n/2} (saddle n=1 -> e^{-i*pi/2}); NEVER real-sqrt a negative macro magnification (use 1/sqrt(gamma^2-(1-kappa)^2)); gamma' (reduced shear = gamma/(1-kappa)) vs gamma naming explicit; use a well-conditioned quartic solver near caustic and near gamma'->1. Do NOT touch operator.py, _hyp1f1.py, or any refusal constant.
  Who: Coder
  Verification: geometry.macro_matrix accepts positive parity byte-identically and saddles (1-kappa<|gamma|, lam>0), and raises the named refusal for lam<=0/Type III and for the float64-exact parity boundary; _centered_source_images returns the correct saddle image set and Morse indices; critical_point/_caustic_source/nearest_caustic_point emit two distinct 3-cusp deltoid lobes from the +- astroid branch with positive-parity output unchanged; Hessian/delay/Morse/image_kernel remain unedited; a saddle-source census yields index sum -2 with image counts strictly in {2,4}.
  Max turns: 90

### WP2: Schwinger 1D dd-quadrature saddle evaluator + parity dispatch (positive path frozen)
  What: Add the NEW certified saddle wave-branch evaluator cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/_schwinger.py (exact 1D Schwinger-parameter dd quadrature, certified-or-refuse, w<=60 ceiling) and wire parity dispatch into operator.F_op/F_op_grid and select_branch, keeping the entire positive-parity path bit-identical to baseline HEAD 3b3ebdb.
  Where: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/_schwinger.py (new), cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/operator.py, cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/_dd.py (only if a missing dd primitive is needed)
  How: FIRST read negative_parity_research.md Sec 6 (exact Schwinger integrand + dd quadrature + paired-rule error estimate), Sec 8 (anchors), Sec 9 (ceiling/refusals); verify pins, do NOT re-derive the formula. (A) _schwinger.py: implement the EXACT 1D Schwinger-parameter representation of F(w,gamma',y), valid at both parities. dd arithmetic is MANDATORY for the quadrature when w>1 — NO float64 quadrature path may exist (float64 silently fabricates past w~20, the saddle analog of F005 -> F005-S; do not retry Pade resummation of the shear series either, a documented dead end). Regularize the integrand endpoints (substitution for any s=0 integrable singularity; controlled decay/truncation at large s) IDENTICALLY across both paired rules. (B) Certify-or-refuse: use PAIRED quadrature rules (two rules sharing the same domain treatment, e.g. Gauss-Kronrod-style or N/2N Gauss-Legendre); accept iff relative paired residual |I_hi-I_lo|/max(|I_hi|,1e-15) < ~1e-11 (one decade below the 1e-10 target, per Professor); else raise a NAMED refusal. HARD CEILING: w>60 -> named refusal, never compute (L_S=pi*w/4 is y-INDEPENDENT, so no explicit y/gamma' ceiling is needed; the paired residual covers near-caustic/near-boundary amplitude effects). Reuse operator.CancellationError or a clearly-named Schwinger refusal — never NaN, never a silent wrong number. (C) numba-njit the dd/quadrature core with .py_func exposure (F010); if a needed dd primitive (dd_exp/dd_log/complex mul) is absent from _dd.py, ADD it there (do NOT duplicate) with njit + .py_func. (D) operator.py parity dispatch: in BOTH F_op and F_op_grid, use geometry's WP1 parity classification to route saddle configs to _schwinger; positive-parity outputs MUST be bit-identical to baseline. PREFERRED design (Professor Option A): extract/keep the positive-parity computation as its OWN frozen njit function called by a thin Python dispatch wrapper, so njit recompilation cannot perturb positive-parity float64 outputs; freeze every positive-parity refusal constant. (E) select_branch: add the saddle w-ceiling condition PARITY-GATED (early parity check) so positive-parity branch selection returns byte-identical results and constants. Conventions: gamma' vs gamma naming explicit; Morse phase e^{-i*pi/2} consistent with cogwheel's Fourier convention; never real-sqrt a negative macro magnification. (F) MEASUREMENT (report, do not gate): record the warm per-point cost (ms/point) of F_schwinger over a small (w,gamma',y) grid in the change report using the same warm-timing discipline as test_lensing_ratio_layer — it prices the envelope-surrogate decision.
  Who: Coder
  Dependencies: WP1
  Verification: cogwheel/lensing/chang_refsdal/_schwinger.py exposes a dd 1D-quadrature evaluator certified-or-refused by paired quadrature rules (accept ~1e-11) with a hard w<=60 named refusal and NO float64 quadrature path; any new dd primitive lives in _dd.py with .py_func exposure; operator.F_op and F_op_grid route saddle configs to the evaluator while positive-parity outputs are bit-identical to baseline HEAD 3b3ebdb and all positive-parity refusal constants are frozen; select_branch's saddle w-ceiling condition is parity-gated with byte-identical positive-parity dispatch; the warm per-point cost is recorded in the change report.
  Max turns: 135

### Professor Inputs
  - Schwinger certify-or-refuse: the hard w<=60 ceiling guards the y-independent oscillatory channel L_S=pi*w/4 (at w=60, L_S~47, dd's ~31 digits give ~16 digits headroom over the 1e-10 target) but is NOT sufficient alone — a paired-rule relative residual with acceptance tau_accept~1e-11 (one decade below target) is the MANDATORY runtime certifier; it also catches near-caustic/near-boundary amplitude concentration, so no explicit y/gamma' ceiling is needed. Refuse (named error) rather than fabricate.
  - Gate-2 grid ~600 points (w in {0.1,0.5,1,5,10,20,30,45,55,60} x gamma' in {1.05,1.2,1.5,2.0,3.0,5.0} x y configs incl on-axis and near-caustic), tolerance 1e-10 uniform with NO degradation near the ceiling; the oracle must be an independent high-dps mpmath 1D-representation, never the production path (F002).
  - Deep-band Morse phase must be pinned as the INTERCEPT phi_0 of the fit phi(w)=phi_0 + a*w*ln(w/2) + b*w (pointwise fails because w*ln w is non-analytic at 0): phi_0 = -pi/2 within 2e-4 and a~1/2; magnitude |F| -> 1/sqrt(gamma^2-(1-kappa)^2)=sqrt(|mu_macro|) with relative error < C*w (C~O(1) by fit). The -pi/2 is the saddle Morse index n=1 factor e^{-i*pi/2}=-i, tied to cogwheel's Fourier sign convention.
  - Census sign convention is (-1)^{n_j} (minimum +1, saddle -1); index sum = -2 for saddle hosts; image counts strictly {2,4} with Morse multisets {1,1} or {0,1,1,1}; the scan MUST include on-axis (y=0), on-caustic on both lobes, near-caustic +-1e-4, near-boundary gamma'=1.001, and a distant source — the regimes that stress the quartic solver.
  - Parity dispatch: prefer Option A — split F_op into a FROZEN positive-parity njit function plus a new saddle function behind a thin Python dispatch wrapper — to guarantee bit-identical positive parity under njit recompilation; do NOT modify the positive-parity select_branch path (parity-gate the new saddle ceiling); enforce with an np.array_equal regression against baseline HEAD 3b3ebdb.
  - Mass-sheet identity must be tested branch-wise on OBSERVABLES (flux ratios, time-delay differences) at 1e-16 geometric and 1e-10 wave, never the code's own rescaling path (F002); lam<=0 is a named refusal.
  - Convention traps to embed in the WPs: Morse phase e^{-i*pi/2} sign vs Fourier convention; never real-sqrt a negative macro magnification (use 1/sqrt(gamma^2-(1-kappa)^2)); gamma' (reduced shear) vs gamma naming; well-conditioned quartic near caustic/boundary; dd is MANDATORY (float64 fabricates past w~20); F010 py_func-chain for every new njit; regularize the Schwinger integrand endpoints identically across both paired rules.
  - Scope caveat flagged (document, don't fix here): w<=60 corresponds to ~25 Hz for a 30 Msun lens, so the saddle wave branch covers only the low-frequency inspiral — Build 7 PE integration must band-limit or refuse above the cutoff; the v-plane steepest-descent ceiling-lift is the deferred alternative.

### Domain Test Descriptions
  - GATE 1 — Census / index theorem (saddle geometry). Setup: >=5 saddle macro configs (kappa,gamma): (0.0,1.05),(0.0,1.5),(0.0,3.0),(0.3,1.0),(0.5,0.8) (all 1-kappa<|gamma|, lam>0), each scanned over ~36 source positions (|y| in {0,0.05,0.1,0.3,0.5,1.0,2.0,5.0} x angle in {0,pi/6,pi/3,pi/2,2pi/3}) for ~200 sources total, PLUS mandatory edge cases: on-axis y=0 for every config, on-caustic on EACH of the two deltoid lobes, just-inside/just-outside each caustic at |y-y_caustic|=1e-4, near-boundary gamma'=1.001, and a distant source |y|=10. Operation: solve the lens equation and compute Morse indices of all images. Expected: image count strictly in {2,4}; sum of (-1)^{n_j} = -2 for EVERY source (no anomalies); if 2 images both have Morse index 1; if 4 images the Morse-index multiset is {0,1,1,1}. Diagnostic: histogram of index sums (a delta at -2); scatter of image positions colored by Morse index near a caustic crossing.
  - GATE 2 — Schwinger accuracy vs an INDEPENDENT mpmath dev-oracle (F002). Setup: an independent high-dps (>=50 dps) mpmath implementation of the 1D Schwinger representation, with an AST import-guard forbidding it (or the test) from importing cogwheel._schwinger/operator/channels (per the committed test_lensing_gauge.py idiom) so the oracle is never the production path. Grid ~600 points: w in {0.1,0.5,1,5,10,20,30,45,55,60}, gamma' in {1.05,1.2,1.5,2.0,3.0,5.0} (including the near-boundary 1.05 that kills the shear series), y configs = {|y|=0} + {|y| in {0.1,0.5,1.0}} x {angle in {0,pi/4,pi/2}}. Operation: compare production F_schwinger to the oracle. Expected: |F-F_oracle|/max(|F_oracle|,1e-15) < 1e-10 at EVERY in-domain point (all w<=60 accepted), uniform, no degradation near the ceiling. Diagnostic: rel-error heatmap over (w,gamma').
  - GATE 3 — Independent 2D rotated-contour oracle anchor (triangle of trust). Setup: read negative_parity_research.md Sec 8 for the exact anchor saddle point (w,gamma',y) and its certified F value; implement a fully INDEPENDENT 2D rotated-contour high-dps mpmath evaluation of the Kirchhoff diffraction integral (a different method from the 1D representation) at that one point, guarded from importing production code. Operation: compare F_schwinger to the 2D-contour oracle. Expected: agreement at the ~2.2e-15 machine-precision class quoted by the research. Diagnostic: report abs and rel difference against the anchor.
  - GATE 4 — Mass-sheet identity on OBSERVABLES, branch-wise (lam>0). Setup: a reference saddle config plus MST-transformed configs with lam in {0.5,0.8,1.2,2.0} (all lam>0). Operation: (geometric branch) compute flux ratios |mu_i/mu_j| and time-delay DIFFERENCES Delta_t_ij for original and transformed; (wave branch) compute |F|^2 / the MST relation at a w grid {1,5,10,20,40}. Expected: geometric observables agree to 1e-16 relative; the wave-branch MST identity holds to 1e-10; computed ONLY on observables (flux ratios, delay differences), NEVER the code's own kappa-rescaling path (F002); the two branches tested separately ('branch-wise'). Also: lam<=0 raises the named refusal. Diagnostic: residual vs lam for each observable.
  - GATE 5 — Deep-band magnitude + Morse-phase (F009-S). Setup: deep-band w in {0.01,0.02,0.05,0.1,0.2} across several saddle (kappa,gamma). Operation: evaluate F. Expected magnitude: |F| -> 1/sqrt(gamma^2-(1-kappa)^2) = sqrt(|mu_macro|), with relative magnitude error < C*w (fit C~O(1) by linear regression, intercept consistent with zero to <1e-4). Expected phase: fit phi(w)=phi_0 + a*w*ln(w/2) + b*w (NOT pointwise — w*ln w is non-analytic at w=0); require phi_0 = -pi/2 within 2e-4 and a consistent with 1/2. Include an explicit check that the negative macro magnification is handled via 1/sqrt(gamma^2-(1-kappa)^2) (never a real sqrt of a negative). Diagnostic: |F| vs w with the sqrt(|mu_macro|) asymptote; unwrapped phase vs w with the fit and the -pi/2 intercept marker.
  - GATE 6 — Wave-branch vs geometric-branch agreement at resolved w. Setup: a saddle config in the resolved regime (w*dtau ~ 5, moderate w). Operation: compare the Schwinger wave-branch F to the stationary-phase geometric sum over real saddle images built from the UNMODIFIED image_kernel on the indefinite Hessian. Expected: agreement ~2.3e-4 at w*dtau~5, improving as w increases. Diagnostic: |F_wave - F_geom| vs w*dtau on a log axis.
  - GATE 7 — Positive-parity byte-identity regression (frozen path). Setup: a positive-parity grid (gamma'<1, 1-kappa>|gamma|) covering F_op and F_op_grid; generate reference outputs from BASELINE HEAD 3b3ebdb (e.g. via `git show 3b3ebdb:...`/a clean baseline checkout) and commit them as a fixture. Operation: evaluate F_op/F_op_grid on the identical grid post-build. Expected: np.array_equal (bit-for-bit) with the baseline fixture; all positive-parity refusal constants unchanged; the full existing lensing suite still green. Diagnostic: count of differing entries (must be exactly 0).
  - SCHWINGER certify-or-refuse contract (refusal symmetry, named-never-silent). Setup: (a) certified in-domain points; (b) w just above the ceiling (60.0001, 65, 80); (c) a deliberately under-resolved paired rule / perturbed acceptance threshold. Operation: call the evaluator. Expected: w<=60 returns a finite certified value; w>60 raises the NAMED refusal (never NaN, never a silent finite-but-wrong value); the falsification perturbation makes the paired-rule certifier REFUSE (goes red), proving the certifier is load-bearing. Diagnostic: table of w vs returned/refused.
  - dd-MANDATORY falsification (F005-S). Setup: run the Schwinger integrand in float64 vs dd at w in {25,30,45}. Operation: compare each to the mpmath oracle. Expected: the float64 path disagrees from dd/oracle by >1e-3 at w>=~25-30 (demonstrating float64 fabrication), while dd matches the oracle to 1e-10 — establishing that dd is load-bearing and no float64 quadrature path may ship. Diagnostic: rel-error vs w overlay for float64 vs dd.
  - F010 njit py_func-chain falsification (all new njit in _schwinger.py and any new _dd primitive). Setup: for each new njit function, patch the ENTIRE call chain to its .py_func body (per F010 idiom — patching only the outer function is insufficient when it calls other njit functions via module globals). Operation: (a) compiled vs full py_func chain agree to float64-exact (np.testing.assert_array_equal); (b) inject a broken constant/branch into the py_func chain and confirm a sensitivity/falsification test goes RED. Expected: compiled==py_func exactly; the broken variant fails. Diagnostic: per-function pass/fail table.
  - Parity classification & dispatch routing (F004 boundary discipline). Setup: (kappa,gamma) points across positive parity (1-kappa>|gamma|), saddle (1-kappa<|gamma|, lam>0), lam<=0/Type III, and the EXACT parity boundary using float64-exact powers-of-two values (kappa=0.5/gamma=0.5, kappa=0.75/gamma=0.25). Operation: call macro_matrix/the parity classifier and F_op. Expected: positive parity -> existing (frozen) path; saddle -> _schwinger; lam<=0/Type III and the exact boundary -> named LensDomainError refusal (never a silent value). Diagnostic: a (kappa,gamma) -> route/refuse table.

